---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  path="/privacy"
  title="Privacy - Nuthatch"
  description="What Nuthatch keeps when you use the site, the hosted demo MCP endpoint, or Nuthatch on your own machine."
>
  <section class="page">
    <article class="wrap narrow prose">
      <p class="section-label">Privacy</p>
      <h1>What we keep</h1>

      <p>
        This page is a record of what Nuthatch keeps, not a legal policy. It covers the website,
        the hosted demo the Claude plugin directory edition talks to, and Nuthatch running on
        your own machine.
      </p>

      <h2>The website</h2>
      <p>
        This site loads no third-party scripts or fonts, and sets no cookies. Page views are
        counted by Vercel Web Analytics, from this origin. Vercel hosts the site and keeps its
        own request logs; we do not control those.
      </p>

      <h2>The hosted demo MCP endpoint</h2>
      <p>
        The Claude plugin directory edition talks to a public, read-only demo nest at
        <a href="https://arc.nuthatch-indexer.com/mcp">https://arc.nuthatch-indexer.com/mcp</a>
        (USDC on Arc testnet). A request there sends the MCP call — the tool name and its
        arguments, including any SQL — over HTTPS, together with ordinary HTTP headers. The nest
        has to receive that call in order to answer it. The data on the nest is public demo data,
        not yours.
      </p>
      <p>
        The reverse proxy in front of the nest writes an access log in nginx's combined format,
        tagged <code>nuthatch_public</code>, to the host's journal. That log holds the caller's IP
        address, the request line (method, path, and any query string), the status code, and the
        <code>Referer</code> and <code>User-Agent</code> headers. It does not include the POST
        body, so the JSON of a <code>POST /mcp</code> tool call is not in the access log. A GET
        with a query string can include a SQL statement (for example
        <code>GET /sql?q=...</code>).
      </p>
      <p>
        Caddy, which terminates TLS for this name, is configured without an access log for the
        site. The nest process is not started with <code>--audit-log</code>, so it does not keep
        a call audit log of statements or MCP arguments.
      </p>
      <p>
        The journal is capped at 1&nbsp;GB on that host, with no fixed time retention configured.
        The same records are also forwarded to the host syslog, which is rotated weekly and kept
        for four rotations.
      </p>

      <h2>Local Nuthatch</h2>
      <p>
        <code>nuthatch mcp</code> on your machine talks to a nest you run, and sends nothing to
        us. The Claude Code marketplace edition of the plugin starts that local server, and does
        not use the hosted demo.
      </p>
      <p>
        The only thing the Nuthatch binary will send to us is the optional
        <a href="/count">head count</a>, off until you say yes.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions or requests: open an issue at
        <a href="https://github.com/nuthatch-org/nuthatch/issues" rel="noopener">github.com/nuthatch-org/nuthatch/issues</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem) clamp(4rem, 9vw, 6.5rem); }
  .prose h1 { margin-bottom: 1.8rem; }
  .prose h2 { margin: 2rem 0 0.8rem; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .prose p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
  .prose p:first-of-type { color: var(--text); }
</style>
